| # | Attraction / Activity | What it is | Approx. price (USD) | Why it’s a good pick for a Hamilton fan |
|---|-----------------------|------------|--------------------|----------------------------------------|
| 1 | **“Hamilton” – the Broadway musical** (Richard Rodgers Theatre, Lincoln Center) | The original Tony‑award‑winning production that started the whole phenomenon. | **$150 – $250** (standard tickets) | The definitive experience – you’ll see the show exactly as Lin‑Manuel intended. |
| 2 | **Hamilton Broadway Backstage & Talk‑Back Tour** | A 45‑minute guided tour of the theatre’s backstage area plus a short Q&A with a former cast member. | **$85 – $120** | Gives you insider stories and a peek behind the curtain without sitting through the full performance. |
| 3 | **Hamilton‑Themed Walking Tour of Lower Manhattan** (e.g., “Alexander Hamilton & the Founding Fathers” tour) | A 2‑hour walking tour that visits the real‑life sites that inspired the musical – Trinity Church, Wall Street, the Alexander Hamilton U.S. Custom House, etc. | **$55 – $70** per person | Connects the history in the show to the actual streets of Manhattan – perfect for a child who loves the story. |
| 4 | **“Hamilton” Exhibit at the New‑York Historical Society** | A temporary museum exhibition that displays original costumes, set pieces, handwritten notes from Lin‑Manuel, and interactive stations where visitors can try out “duel” choreography or record a short rap verse. | **$30 – $40** (adult ticket) | **Under $45** – a hands‑on, affordable way to dive into the world of Hamilton without buying a theater ticket. |
| 5 | **Hamilton‑Inspired Kids’ Workshop – Children’s Museum of Manhattan** | A 90‑minute, age‑appropriate workshop (ages 5‑12) that teaches the story of the American Revolution through music, lyric‑writing, and a mini‑stage‑building activity. | **$20 – $25** per child | Fun, educational, and budget‑friendly – great for a younger fan. |
| 6 | **Free Hamilton‑themed Street Performances** (summer festivals, Times Square) | Short, high‑energy renditions of the show’s most famous numbers performed by professional buskers. | **Free** (tips optional) | A quick, no‑cost way to enjoy a taste of the music while exploring the city. |

### ✅ The option that meets your price requirement
**The “Hamilton” Exhibit at the New‑York Historical Society** is the first Hamilton‑themed activity on the list that costs **under $45** (adult tickets are $30‑$40).  

**What you’ll get:**  

* Authentic costumes, props, and handwritten lyric sheets from the Broadway production.  
* Interactive stations where visitors can try on a “duel” sword, record a short rap verse, or explore a digital timeline of Alexander Hamilton’s life.  
* A short documentary video that explains the real‑life history behind the characters.  

**How to book / visit:**  

1. **Check the dates** – The exhibit runs on a rotating schedule, so verify that it’s open on the dates you plan to be in New York (the Historical Society’s website lists current and upcoming exhibitions).  
2. **Buy tickets** – Purchase tickets online at the New‑York Historical Society’s site or at the museum’s box office.  
3. **Plan your visit** – The museum is located at **170 Central Park West (near the American Museum of Natural History)**. Allocate about **1.5‑2 hours** for the Hamilton exhibit, plus extra time if you want to explore the museum’s other galleries.  

If you’d like more details on any of the other options (e.g., show times for the Broadway production, how to join the walking tour, or scheduling the kids’ workshop), just let me know and I can pull the exact dates, availability, and booking links for you. Enjoy the Hamilton adventure in the city that inspired it!

